WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.624
Good morning, it's Monday, November 16.

00:00:02.691 --> 00:00:09.756
This is Signal in the AI Fog, your daily briefing on enterprise AI in production, written and read by AI.

00:00:09.823 --> 00:00:18.973
Today: Anthropic's IPO ties it to two clouds, Nvidia reports earnings without Jensen Huang, and Gemini 2.5 Pro reroute changes the bill.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.924
First, the story of the day.

00:00:20.991 --> 00:00:34.918
Anthropic said on Thursday that it will price its initial public offering on Wednesday, November eighteenth, and begin trading on Nasdaq as A N T on Thursday, November nineteenth, according to Yahoo Finance.

00:00:34.986 --> 00:00:44.203
The offer is 825 million shares at seventy to seventy-eight dollars each, up to about sixty-four billion dollars at the top of the range.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:55.237
A Saturday KuCoin report says a concurrent twenty-six billion dollar private placement involves AMD, Broadcom, Google, Micron, Microsoft, Nvidia and TSMC Partners.

00:00:55.304 --> 00:00:58.937
Yahoo says Nvidia's part is up to ten billion dollars.

00:00:59.004 --> 00:01:10.913
NBC News, reporting on the filing, says Anthropic plans to spend one hundred fifteen billion dollars with Google and forty-five billion with Microsoft on computing through 2033.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:16.430
It also reports a first-half 2026 net loss of eighty point seven billion dollars.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:22.091
What this really signals: the supplier is raising money from its own suppliers.

00:01:22.155 --> 00:01:29.061
Chip makers and clouds become shareholders, and two of those clouds also hold the large compute commitments.

00:01:29.125 --> 00:01:37.054
For a platform team, that means Claude capacity, pricing and availability are likely tied to Google and Microsoft decisions.

00:01:37.118 --> 00:01:39.868
Check which cloud route your contracts use.

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:44.408
Rehearse a failover through your gateway before Thursday, and time it.

00:01:44.472 --> 00:01:51.441
Once the stock trades, vendor risk will be discussed quarter after quarter, so put a review in your calendar.

00:01:51.505 --> 00:01:55.150
Treat valuation headlines as noise for routing decisions.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.387
Next, Models and vendors.

00:01:57.453 --> 00:02:08.652
According to migration guides citing Google's deprecations page, from December first all requests to Gemini 2.5 Pro are routed to Gemini 3.8 Flash and billed at its rates.

00:02:08.717 --> 00:02:15.856
That is seventy-five cents per million input tokens and three dollars seventy-five per million output tokens.

00:02:15.921 --> 00:02:23.191
Gemini 2.5 Pro costs one dollar twenty-five per million input tokens and ten dollars per million output tokens.

00:02:23.256 --> 00:02:27.120
Gemini 2.5 Flash moves to 3.5 Flash-Lite at the same price.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.831
The read here: the bill falls, but so does the model tier.

00:02:31.902 --> 00:02:37.784
A Pro workload answered by a Flash model is a quality question, not a savings line.

00:02:37.855 --> 00:02:45.510
Run your evaluation set against 3.8 Flash before December first, and have the gateway flag the substitution.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:47.978
Next, Sovereignty and Europe.

00:02:48.043 --> 00:02:53.583
Two model trackers say Mistral Large 4 reached general availability on November fifth.

00:02:53.647 --> 00:02:59.445
It entered public preview on October sixth, and open weights are reported on Hugging Face.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:06.274
One tracker describes it as a one trillion parameter multimodal model trained on European infrastructure.

00:03:06.338 --> 00:03:10.590
I could not open Mistral's own page, so treat this as unconfirmed.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:20.727
Why it matters: if confirmed, Europe has a large open-weight model you can also host yourself, which strengthens a sovereign route in the gateway.

00:03:20.792 --> 00:03:29.610
Verify licence terms, hardware needs and price on Mistral's pages, then benchmark on your own tasks before calling it production-ready.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.135
Next, Platform.

00:03:31.197 --> 00:03:39.090
According to Forbes and Benzinga, Jensen Huang resigned as Nvidia's chief executive last week, and Colette Kress is interim CEO.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:45.257
Forbes reports a Justice Department probe and a stock drop of almost thirteen percent for the week.

00:03:45.318 --> 00:03:51.485
Nvidia reports quarterly earnings on Tuesday, November seventeenth, its first since the resignation.

00:03:51.547 --> 00:03:54.630
Analysts expect two dollars forty-seven per share.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:59.777
Reading between the lines: nothing changes in your clusters this week.

00:03:59.842 --> 00:04:04.648
But guidance on supply and roadmap will shape inference cost expectations.

00:04:04.713 --> 00:04:13.352
For a platform team, the lasting question is dependence: how much of your serving stack is tied to one accelerator vendor's software?

00:04:13.416 --> 00:04:15.430
Watch any change in lead times.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.460
Next, Retail and agents.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:24.254
Walmart said in October that Agent Profiles, a dedicated identity for each shopping agent, launch within a month.

00:04:24.314 --> 00:04:30.929
PYMNTS reports customers can cap spending at fifty, one hundred or two hundred dollars, or approve every order.

00:04:30.989 --> 00:04:39.869
Home Depot's chief information officer told Business Insider the retailer will admit agents that identify themselves and the customer they represent.

00:04:39.929 --> 00:04:42.670
It is in talks with Meta about its Muse agent.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:50.656
What this really signals: retailers are writing admission rules, not simply blocking or opening the door.

00:04:50.727 --> 00:04:59.098
For a retailer, the work is on your side: agent identity, per-agent limits, and logs of which agent placed which order.

00:04:59.168 --> 00:05:03.600
Product data and APIs must be agent-ready before the rules are.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.621
The number of the day.

00:05:05.686 --> 00:05:15.506
December second is the date by which generative systems already on the market before August second must meet the AI Act's machine-readable marking duty.

00:05:15.571 --> 00:05:16.475
What to watch.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:23.323
Microsoft Ignite runs November seventeenth to twentieth, with Satya Nadella's keynote on the seventeenth.

00:05:23.388 --> 00:05:30.947
Nvidia reports earnings that day, and Google's Sovereign AI Summit starts as several Gemini audio previews shut down.

00:05:31.011 --> 00:05:40.185
Anthropic prices its IPO November eighteenth and trades November nineteenth, the day of OVHcloud's summit and the Gemini 3.6 Flash retirement.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:44.191
Walmart's Agent Profiles are due about November twenty-first.

00:05:44.255 --> 00:05:50.135
Next comes the Gemini 2.5 reroute on December first, and AI Act marking on December second.

00:05:50.199 --> 00:05:52.073
And a question for your team.

00:05:52.137 --> 00:06:02.603
If your main model supplier's investors are also your cloud providers, does your risk register show that dependency, and has anyone timed a failover this quarter?

00:06:02.668 --> 00:06:03.960
That's it for today.

00:06:04.025 --> 00:06:06.544
Sources are in the episode description.

00:06:06.609 --> 00:06:08.547
This was Signal in the AI Fog.

00:06:08.612 --> 00:06:09.710
See you tomorrow.
